WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:02.866
(bell dinging)

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.006
- Hello, everyone, Sal
here, sorry. (laughs)

00:00:23.006 --> 00:00:26.120
So this is a very makeshift situation

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.220
that we're dealing with.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.810
I've moved locations.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.060
Yesterday, the Internet
connection wasn't so good.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.960
I think it because I was
away from the Wi-Fi router,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.230
so now I'm in my mother-in-law's bedroom

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.420
who lives with us.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.150
And it is closer to the Wi-Fi routers.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.620
So hopefully all of this is going to be

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.683
a little bit smoother today.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.232
Welcome, I guess you
could say live stream.

00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:48.920
That's how people have started calling it,

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.310
a home room of sorts just to
get us started on the day.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.770
For those of you who are new,

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.730
the goal of this is really
just to be a resource

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.460
for parents, for teachers,
and for students.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.870
All of us are trying to navigate

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.150
this whole situation
that we find ourselves in

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.520
where we have school
closures around the country

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.900
and around the world.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.410
I think I saw data yesterday

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.050
that there's 900 (distorted speaking)

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:13.730
around the world that
would normally be in school

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.700
but who aren't in school right now.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.180
And all of us at Khan Academy,

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.610
we realize that we would
have never foreseen

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:24.600
this type of a situation, but we exist

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.740
to help out a situation like this.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.060
All of our entire team at Khan Academy,

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.620
I really wanna thank everyone
on Khan Academy's team

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:31.927
and all of the supporters of Khan Academy

00:01:31.927 --> 00:01:34.630
and our volunteers and
our teacher ambassadors

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:37.320
for really stepping up
over the last few days.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.580
I've been mentioning this every day,

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.000
but some of the core resources
that we've been putting out,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.270
other than doing this daily live stream,

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.960
or home room, if you will,

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.350
we've been putting out teacher webinars

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.070
to help teachers get signed up.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.810
We've been seeing record number

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.250
of registrations of teachers.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.190
It looks like some might
even be a factor of 10.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.030
At least that's what
one of my team members

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.720
told me earlier this morning.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.300
We're seeing a record number
of registration of parents

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.850
who are running parent webinars

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.540
to help parents get set up.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.260
Over the weekend, we realized that

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.100
we have a lot of resources at Khan Academy

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.650
that cover all of the
major subjects and grades,

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.210
but parents and teachers
who are now looking

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.760
to virtualize need to know,

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.010
well, how do I structure the
day so it feels like school?

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.880
And obviously, this is
a substitute for it,

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.890
and this is a very suboptimal situation.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.810
We released schedules that
work for students as young

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:32.820
as pre-K going into kindergarten,
first, second grade.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.270
Then we have a schedule
for elementary age,

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.700
schedule for middle and high school,

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.700
and then schedule for later high school

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.690
across subjects and grades so that people

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.090
know how to structure their day.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.320
And it's not just do this
thing on Khan Academy

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.430
or that thing on Khan Academy.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.650
There are breaks scheduled in.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.500
There's even some resources we, or recess,

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.970
one of my family friends immediately

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:56.160
when she saw that it had
Yoga with Adriene on it,

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.520
and Just Dance, she's, those are two

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.470
of my favorite exercise activities

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.580
when it's a rainy day
and I can't go outside.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.500
So yes, I had a little bit
of editorial influence,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.530
but those are resources for all of you.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.810
We're doing this live stream.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.670
Expect over the coming days and weeks

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.030
to see more live streams
that maybe spawn off of this.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.770
We're exploring ways to provide

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.470
teachers and students and
parents more supports.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.070
One idea that we've talked about,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.010
and I've talked about this yesterday,

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.230
is as you go through those schedules

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.900
of leveraging Khan Academy
and other resources,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.900
if teachers could set up a webinar

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.630
or video conferencing for their students,

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.350
that way the students could log in

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.370
while they're obviously
working on Khan Academy math

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.820
or biology, and then ask questions,

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.300
students could also
self-organize around that.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.300
And if folks are still
just getting off the ground

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.170
and parents could also.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.430
The other thing I really wanna
emphasize for everyone is

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.080
don't stress out about the situation.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.553
We're really just at the beginning

00:03:55.553 --> 00:03:59.030
of a situation that's
very new to all of us.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.640
And so, even if it takes several days

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.390
going into next week to
get everyone into a rhythm,

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.650
that's completely understandable.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.210
In my house, we have had situation.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.150
I had to hush my children outside

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.910
as they were screaming
over, fighting over a chair

00:04:16.073 --> 00:04:17.950
for eating breakfast.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.560
This is an interesting
situation for all of us.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.410
And we just saw news last night,

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.100
we've been talking about
something like this,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.870
if you just look at the,
what's been happening

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.090
in other countries and when
you might hit peak virus

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.430
or peak infection, it
looks like it's going to be

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.930
more than just a few weeks.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:40.850
Several school districts, the
team tells me I think Kansas,

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.053
let me make sure I'm getting that right,

00:04:46.127 --> 00:04:48.700
announced, yeah, it says
Kansas is the first state

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.500
to close schools for the
rest of the academic year.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.440
We have about 2 1/2 months
in the academic year,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.930
and so that probably will be
extended for a lot of folks.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.280
I think all of us need to figure out

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.750
how do we work together to make sure

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.260
that everyone keeps learning,
not just through the rest

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.610
of the academic year, but then we can

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.460
leverage summer as well
to keep that learning

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.860
so that as we go into
the new school year where

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:11.913
hopefully everything is fine by then,

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.950
everyone is ready and capable to engage.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.310
And if, for whatever reason,

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.973
this whole situation comes back,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:27.233
we know how to switch between
these modalities quite fast.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.520
Let me look at some
questions that are here.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.880
One question was, are we able

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.030
to meet increased demands,

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.420
or are we seeing any increased demands?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:40.840
What the team at Khan Academy has told me,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.510
on Monday we saw a 50% increase in traffic

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.500
from the Monday previous,
and it looks like Tuesday,

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.390
yesterday, was even higher than Monday.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.510
And so we're still looking at
the data, but it looks like

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.710
there's a pretty dramatic
increase in demand.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:56.640
And obviously, there's an increased demand

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.220
for this type of thing, for us to be able

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.750
to help people navigate the entire crisis.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.240
I wanna make a huge shout out,

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.650
for those of you who haven't seen it,

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.170
there was a press release last night,

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:10.240
Bank of America I wanna
thank operation to step up.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.950
We've had a long standing
relationship with Bank of America.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:16.010
They've been the main partner

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:17.700
for our financial literacy content,

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:21.460
for our career content
over the past seven years,

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.250
and the reason why Khan Academy has even

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.630
been able to step up in this crisis

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:27.530
is because of many years of support

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.670
from folks like Bank of America.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:33.270
But as soon as Thursday
and Friday of last week,

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.230
they saw that this is going to be

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.250
a bit of a situation
around the school closures.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:41.350
They immediately saw us as
a really instrumental part

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.120
of this, and they called us up and said,

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.730
what can we do to help?

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.140
We wanna make sure that America

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.120
and the world can keep learning.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.220
And over the weekend,
they've provided resources

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.810
for Khan Academy so that we
could keep our servers up,

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.130
so we can do this type of live stream.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:01.370
We're calling it a national,
or international home room.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.080
They've provided, they're
gonna help provide awareness

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:06.940
so that parents, teachers, students

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.870
around the country who might not be aware

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:11.270
of Khan Academy or the
resources we're providing

00:07:12.601 --> 00:07:15.351
over this, I guess you could
call it social distancing,

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:19.243
that we're able to provide
more of those resources

00:07:19.243 --> 00:07:21.890
that we have the aperture to think bigger

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.930
about how we can solve things.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:26.130
And they also have a lot
of really good partnerships

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.780
with other nonprofits, school districts,

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.820
solve parts of the situation

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.490
because Khan Academy is a part of it.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.610
We have, obviously we
can do things online.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.210
We have all of this content,
all of this software,

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.190
but above and beyond that,

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.830
we wanna look to partner with folks

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.070
to ensure that all students

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.630
can have access to things
like Internet right now.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.310
That's valuable not just for Khan Academy

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.050
but it's also, I think important

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.830
in this time of social distancing

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.470
to be able to have some social interaction

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.300
that's not traditional social media,

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.950
but you can also interact with
people and things like that.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.610
Thank you so much for Bank of America

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:02.240
for being in record time, stepping up

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.810
to support Khan Academy
so that we can support

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.690
so many others and helping
the support directly.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:11.650
I'd love to answer y'all's questions.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:15.380
Let's see, I can look at
this stream down here,

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:20.380
and I can see what the
team is surfacing to me.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:25.760
There is one question,

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.840
let's see, how do I figure out

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.363
what my child should be learning?

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.010
There's a couple of ways
to think about this.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.040
I actually had a really
great conversation.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.410
Some of you might have seen
the video with Tim Vandenberg,

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.680
who is grade math teacher
in Hesperia, California.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.810
I also learned yesterday,
he's the number two

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.470
Monopoly player in the
country or the world.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:47.840
There's a documentary
about him apparently.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.980
So he's an impressive guy
all around. (laughing)

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.700
And I always thought
Monopoly was mostly luck,

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.730
but I was like, "Can you
always beat me in Monopoly?"

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.730
He was like, "Yes, I will
pretty much always beat you."

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:59.947
And then he said, "My sixth graders

00:08:59.947 --> 00:09:00.920
"will beat you at Monopoly."

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.660
So he knows what he's doing in Monopoly.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.010
And frankly, if we can figure out a way

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.230
to bring in remote guests
on this live stream,

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.127
I would love to bring Tim in.

00:09:10.127 --> 00:09:11.510
But the reason why I brought up Tim

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:14.020
is he has some really great ways

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:17.380
to work with students, gaps
in their knowledge because

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:19.750
there's two views.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.940
One view is, say, okay, we're about 3/4

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.010
through the school year, so therefore,

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:28.810
maybe we should be exactly 3/4
through whatever grade level

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.840
your child is working on.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.210
And there's a lot of truth to that.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:34.030
What Tim Vandenberg has seen is that

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.370
a lot of his students, as they've gone

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:39.380
at a fixed pace for all students,

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.530
they might get a B in one concept,

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.860
so they have a 10% gap,
a C in another concept,

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:46.800
they have a 20% gap, and
those gaps keep accumulating.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.070
And that's why when he
gets them in sixth grade,

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:50.860
oftentimes they have trouble engaging

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.500
in that grade level material.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.160
And so what he does is he
has all of his students,

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.090
these are sixth graders,
start at kindergarten

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.700
on Khan Academy, and do our,

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.357
or actually our Early Learning
section on Khan Academy

00:10:03.357 --> 00:10:06.110
and our Arithmetic
section on Khan Academy,

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:06.970
and our third grade.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.240
Those are the three he
says he has them focus on.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:13.150
And then simultaneously,
he also tries to get them

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.900
to complete unit by unit at sixth grade

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.040
so they're able to be on grade level

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.470
and make sure they have
all their gaps filled.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:23.500
And at his school, in his
school, 90% of the students

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.030
that come to him are
well below grade level.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:27.600
So it's super important for him.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.840
But what he finds is is
by allowing some time

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:34.040
for the students to remediate
or fill in those gaps,

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.340
they're more likely to
really master the concepts

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.560
at the grade level as well.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.973
This is just a long-winded way of saying,

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:42.740
you should absolutely
talk to your student,

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.550
or if you are the student, think about

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:45.730
where you are in the year.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.830
You can start on those
units on Khan Academy,

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.700
but given that we have
more flexibility right now

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.530
given your school day is really defined

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:54.983
by you and your parents and your teachers,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.460
that you could especially in math,

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.540
you could spend a little bit extra time

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.140
where you can do things
at your grade level

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.210
or that at your own time
and pace on Khan Academy.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:07.240
So if you're a sixth grader,
work on the sixth grade math.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.120
You could take the Course Challenge.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.370
The Course Challenge will take
you about 30 or 40 minutes,

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.010
but it'll accelerate the
things that you already know,

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:16.520
and then the things you're
having difficulty with,

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.340
you can go to those units,

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.320
and then you can take the unit test there.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.700
And then on those unit
tests, when you take those,

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.870
you can learn what skills
you might need help on.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.540
And if you do that in sixth grade,

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.170
and then it wouldn't be a bad idea

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.920
to set some other time, maybe
another half an hour a day,

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.920
where you start with early
math on Khan Academy,

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:38.150
go into the arithmetic,
go into third grade

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:39.980
to really make sure you have your basics.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.630
You can use things like
the Course Challenges

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.070
and Unit Tests and the Mastery Challenges

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.160
to accelerate through it.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.900
So it's not going to
take you a lot of time

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:50.710
if you already know all of the materials.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:54.200
Let me look at other courses.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.850
Another thing about the schedule,

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.570
another like what to
work on during the year,

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.710
I think it's important to realize,

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.200
this is for parents as well,

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.610
that if you the student or you the parent,

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:09.890
as long as the student can
focus on the foundations

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:10.723
and really master it.

00:12:10.723 --> 00:12:14.280
So what I've been telling
the press lately is

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.760
we have these schedules that can fill up

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.300
most of what would be the
traditional school hours,

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:21.730
but if you at least do two hours a day,

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:24.390
an hour of reading, an hour of math,

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:25.490
that will get your basics.

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:29.013
Those skills won't atrophy.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.953
Your reading comprehension will keep up,

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:35.430
and your math skills won't go away.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.890
But ideally, you're able
to look at a schedule

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.770
like what we've published

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.810
and modify it to your own needs obviously

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.410
and hopefully make use and
give us feedback on that.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.307
