You're exactly right.

00:13:30.823 --> 00:13:32.660
In the past, for things like SAT and AP,

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:36.200
webinars, live streams, and our team

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.923
is exploring how we can do that.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:42.200
I also want folks who create
video conferencing software,

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:45.250
are there ways to get people
into video conferencing groups

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:46.580
so that they can also help each other?

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:48.930
So we can do these larger
scale live streams,

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:51.120
whether it's from me or other teachers

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.380
or content creators, and
then it would also be great

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.780
if we could find ways for folks
to connect with each other

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.160
and answer each other's questions.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.310
Simple answer is yes.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.790
The plan is there.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.880
Hopefully you'll start
seeing some of that stuff

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:06.140
by next week or even at
the end of this week.

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:08.353
Okay, let's see.

00:14:09.697 --> 00:14:12.587
"It says, on Facebook,
we saw a lot of comments

00:14:12.587 --> 00:14:14.477
"about pursuing passions and hobbies.

00:14:14.477 --> 00:14:16.617
"Is that in the schedule?

00:14:16.617 --> 00:14:19.367
"How important is that?"

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:24.290
This is, passions and hobbies
are a super important thing.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.528
And in some ways, you view this situation

00:14:27.528 --> 00:14:29.530
we find ourselves in as glass half full.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.320
I think especially as
you get into high school,

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:33.100
a lot of students, and
if you are a student,

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.090
I'll talk to you, a lot of you are,

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:38.710
would traditionally have
a lot on your plate.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.250
You're taking six classes.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.690
You're doing all these
extracurricular activities.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:44.050
You're taking the SAT.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.780
You're studying for AP tests.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.770
You're applying to college.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:48.060
It can be pretty stressful.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.090
Now, all of a sudden, a
lot of that is cleared out.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:52.420
And so I think this is
a really powerful time

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:54.190
for you to keep on your academics,

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:56.310
and that's where we've
really gotta help you.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:15:00.070
And also, think, you have
time to pursue your passions.

00:15:00.070 --> 00:15:01.450
It might be creating videos.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:02.500
It might be writing.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.740
It might be software.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.430
It might be dance.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:08.970
And I think creativity is oftentimes

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.447
the byproduct of boredom.

00:15:11.447 --> 00:15:14.040
So if you have a little bit
of time on your hands now,

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.410
really think about what motivates you.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:20.730
And this whole crisis that we're
all going through together,

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.840
there's a lot of new problems

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:24.730
that I think need to be solved,

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.100
and so if you're a student,

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:28.200
think about how you would
solve those problems.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:31.300
Are there new types of
things you can invent

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:33.930
that will lower the spread of the virus

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.313
or that can help people?

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.360
Are there volunteer
efforts that you can do

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.330
even while people are social distanced

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.550
to make sure that maybe members

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:45.020
of your community who
might be living alone,

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:47.030
might not have as much support,

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:50.260
that they are feeling a
connection with other people

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.210
or that they feel supported or people

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:54.990
can help them with their
groceries and things like that?

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:58.020
There's things we have to
think about with the economy.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.550
I'm very fortunate.

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:02.000
I'm continuing to get my salary

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.520
because I can do my work remotely.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.180
There's a lot of folks that now

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:08.560
that there's this social
distancing in place,

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:09.960
California where I live is now

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.910
in full stay in place orders,

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:13.970
there's a lot of people who aren't able

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.130
to make their living right now.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:17.350
Are there creative ideas to how we help

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:18.640
some of those folks?

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.620
Yeah, I think this is a
great time for your passions,

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.550
and you can almost, you
could really view this

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:24.573
as a bit of a opportunity.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:30.650
See, other questions, I keep
having to re-log, let's see.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.367
So Sonya Taburg says, "Sal, you talk

00:16:34.367 --> 00:16:36.627
"about eliminating the
Swiss cheese analogy

00:16:36.627 --> 00:16:39.347
