is something we would love to do.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:57.150
And I hope we can do over time.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:58.980
And I was talking about Tim Vandenberg,

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:01.290
and I talked about his
methodology he uses,

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.910
but he's been seeing incredible results

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.580
where pretty much every one of his,

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.160
he starts the year 90% of his students

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.370
aren't at grade level.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:10.420
He sees pretty much year where 90%

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:13.580
of his students are at
grade level or above

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.210
by the end of the year by making sure

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:17.870
that his students can fill
in their Swiss cheese gaps.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.370
And I'll ask the team to put the link

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:21.810
to the Tim Vandenberg video,

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:25.080
or actually webinar that we
had below in our description

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.340
or in our live stream some place

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:30.190
because not only is it
inspiring for teachers

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.180
to see what Tim's done, I think it can be

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:33.690
very inspiring for parents to say, oh,

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.440
well, now we have an opportunity.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.910
We can do this at home,
leveraging Khan Academy.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.080
It's also hopefully inspiring for students

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.640
to say, oh, maybe this is why

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:42.840
I've been having trouble in algebra.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:44.030
It's not because I'm not bright.

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:45.830
It's not because algebra's difficult.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.050
It's because I had all
these gaps accumulating.

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.640
What Tim says even sixth
graders, seventh graders,

00:17:50.640 --> 00:17:52.260
you start them on that early math,

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.850
third grade math, arithmetic,

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:55.700
they almost always discover,

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.280
even the ones that are A or B students,

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.390
some of the ones who are
performing at grade level,

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:03.980
they discover that they had
some gaps with mathematics.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.163
And so let's see.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:10.477
Let's see, Michael Toscano says,

00:18:10.477 --> 00:18:12.047
"It's probably old at this point,

00:18:12.047 --> 00:18:15.303
"but this time the video really
puts the home in home room!"

00:18:15.303 --> 00:18:16.136
(laughs) Yes, you're right!

00:18:16.136 --> 00:18:18.193
This is a literally a room in my home.

00:18:18.193 --> 00:18:21.951
It is home room, that is correct.

00:18:21.951 --> 00:18:23.770
(distorted speaking) Stuff
going on at her work.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.890
There, he doesn't get exposed somehow

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:27.170
and obviously I have three kids,

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.750
and I have to say, the older two,

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:33.560
our school is doing engage in his work.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.610
Again, it's interesting times.

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.625
I definitely empathize.

00:18:36.625 --> 00:18:37.920
And it's one of these times

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.070
where it's a lot of
gratitude and thankful.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:43.680
It makes you appreciate a
lot of the small things.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.340
I went to the grocery store
this morning at 6:00 AM,

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:47.173
which is when it opened.

00:18:47.173 --> 00:18:48.900
I figured, that might be the best time.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.600
But you can imagine it was already

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:54.760
an interesting place to be.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:58.563
But I felt fortunate
to even be able to go.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.063
Let's see, other questions.

00:19:04.546 --> 00:19:06.597
"Is Khan Academy," this
is from Nolan Fisherman,

00:19:06.597 --> 00:19:08.940
"is Khan Academy enough
to study for the AP exam?"

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:12.223
What is other questions that people have?

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.420
Let's see, just a lot of nice people.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:17.880
Apparently I am lagging.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:18.793
I'm sorry.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:20.663
Give me feedback.

00:19:20.663 --> 00:19:23.543
This is closer to my
Wi-Fi router, we'll see.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.710
Let's see, "do you,"

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.037
so someone says, "do you think scientists

00:19:30.037 --> 00:19:31.837
"will find a cure for COVID-19?

00:19:31.837 --> 00:19:34.290
"If so, when do you think we'll find it?"

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:35.600
I'm not an epidemiologist.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:36.830
I'm not an virologist.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.700
So take all of this with a grain of salt,

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:42.190
but I've taught some of
the things on viruses

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:44.310
and things on Khan Academy.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:46.120
Look, I don't think any of us really know,

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.400
including many of the
experts at this point.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.860
We can only hope.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:51.230
There's some early reports

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:55.450
of doctors using cocktails
of existing drugs

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.040
that have been used for other things,

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:01.750
like malaria or AIDS that
might have some promise to it.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.583
Who knows?

00:20:02.583 --> 00:20:06.190
It's just, we're getting
such distorted reports

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:07.410
from different parts of the world

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:10.310
with very different mortality
rates and infection rates,

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.730
and obviously the testing is a big issue.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.780
The number one thing all of us can do

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:19.780
is minimize contact with
physical contact right now

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:23.020
to try to stay with your family.

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:24.410
I'm really glad that California

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.060
where I live decided to
make the hard decision

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:28.350
of doing the stay in place order.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:29.930
It's hard.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.020
Everyone has to be in their house.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.840
They are allowing that you can go outside

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.820
if you wanna go for a run, but even then,

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:37.130
they say make sure you
keep distances from people.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.160
But this is the kind of
action you need to do,

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:43.550
and in any type of
epidemiological response,

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.590
if you do the right thing,

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:47.430
it will look like you are overly cautious.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.340
But if you aren't overly cautious,

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:51.350
then you see these things
grow exponentially,

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.650
and then it's very hard to stop.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:55.310
And the United States, we are
in an unfortunate situation

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:57.480
where the testing isn't
where it needs to be,

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.680
and so I posted a video
that the likely cases

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:02.650
are far higher, are likely far higher,

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.330
in fact, almost for sure, are far higher

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.950
than the reported cases.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.350
So it's very prudent that in our area,

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.100
the seven counties for
seven million people

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.630
they did the stay in place order.

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.380
I think that will be useful for much

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:14.410
of the rest of the world.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.810
Obviously, it has economic implications,

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:17.643
et cetera, et cetera.

00:21:17.643 --> 00:21:19.750
But it's much better to
nip things in the bud,

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:24.620
and it might be a little bit
past the bud stage right now.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:25.610
We will see.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:26.850
We're all through this together.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:28.150
This is really interesting time.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:30.410
It's a great time to learn
about what a virus is,

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:33.780
what DNA is, what RNA
is, listen to the news,

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.610
learn a lot about how the economy works

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:36.620
'cause people are realizing,

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.500
okay, there's certain roles where people

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.160
are able to have income,
but there's other parts

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.160
of our economy where
people already didn't have

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:45.660
a lot of money, but they're
getting hourly paychecks.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:47.240
Now the restaurants in our area,

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:49.550
all of the restaurants are
closed except for takeout.

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:52.470
How are the owners gonna
have money to pay them?

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.860
And if they don't have money, how are they

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:57.020
going to be able to even
get the basic necessities

00:21:57.020 --> 00:21:58.790
they need or pay rent?

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.320
There's all sorts of interesting ideas

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:02.030
that people are starting to float

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:03.450
on how to get everyone through this.

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:05.910
But I've been proud just
to see how most people

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.230
have been acting in the
collective interest,

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:11.170
which I think is really, really powerful.

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:12.420
Maybe time for a few more questions.

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:13.340
I started late.

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:15.849
And I really enjoy this.

00:22:15.849 --> 00:22:19.750
This is almost a little
bit for my sanity as well.

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:22.240
It feels really nice to feel
even virtually connected

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:26.533
with all of you 'cause I
am also socially distanced.

