00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:46.170
into the engineering field, but long term,

00:22:46.170 --> 00:22:48.200
I hope one day we can
do some of the basics

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:50.840
of some of the engineering fields.

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:55.830
Let's see, other, other,
other, someone said,

00:22:55.830 --> 00:22:59.623
oh, let's see, other
questions people are asking.

00:23:02.047 --> 00:23:03.567
"Any plans on expanding Khan Academy

00:23:03.567 --> 00:23:05.350
"higher studies like engineering?"

00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:07.000
A lot of people want engineering.

00:23:08.210 --> 00:23:10.230
Let's see other questions.

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:13.080
I'll go to see what the team
might have surfaced as well.

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:17.080
There are a lot of comments coming in

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:18.373
on social media as well.

00:23:22.758 --> 00:23:23.753
Anna Murray asked, "Do you things

00:23:24.987 --> 00:23:27.670
"for early learning before first grade?"

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:32.670
And Khan Academy Kids, it's
available on Android and on iOS.

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:33.870
It's free.

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:35.220
Go download it.

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:38.450
What you'll see is when you see most apps

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:40.950
for especially that age
group, they just do one thing.

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:43.360
This app has a little bit
of a universe inside of it.

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:45.700
It has over 100 books,
has hundreds of videos,

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:46.810
and they're interactive videos

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:48.610
where there'll be a song and a dance.

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:50.490
And then they'll stop,
and they'll ask your child

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:52.010
or your student to do something.

00:23:52.010 --> 00:23:55.900
It's appropriate for students
as early as age three.

00:23:55.900 --> 00:23:59.540
In fact, I would say even
potentially for age two.

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:01.560
For that age group, it's always best

00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:04.610
to be able to do it next to
or on the lap of a loved one,

00:24:04.610 --> 00:24:08.680
a parent, an uncle, aunt, a
grandparent, older sibling.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:10.250
But if they're able to do 20 minutes,

00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:12.430
30 minutes a day, I think
they'll really enjoy it.

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.600
And we've seen some promising
efficacy studies around it,

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.470
and it'll get them, it
starts with letters,

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.730
numbers, colors, social,
emotional learning,

00:24:19.730 --> 00:24:22.300
but it goes all the way through
the Head Start Standards,

00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:23.657
the Kindergarten Common Core Standards,

00:24:23.657 --> 00:24:25.900
and the First Grade Common Core Standards.

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:30.690
If you start your child on
it, start in age three, say,

00:24:30.690 --> 00:24:32.123
it has plenty of runway for them

00:24:32.123 --> 00:24:33.670
that it can keep them busy for a while.

00:24:33.670 --> 00:24:35.910
And it adapts to them
based on what they know

00:24:35.910 --> 00:24:38.290
and what they don't know, so
highly, highly encourage that.

00:24:38.290 --> 00:24:39.950
That's why we created Khan Academy Kids.

00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:41.440
We've seen downloads go up.

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:42.640
Last I heard from our team,

00:24:42.640 --> 00:24:45.143
fivefold from what they typically are.

00:24:46.050 --> 00:24:48.860
Hopefully, people are making...

00:24:51.100 --> 00:24:53.853
One foot in front, they are
representing other companies.

